<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine central government deficit falls in May.</title>
<headline>Argentine central government deficit falls in May.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's central government deficit fell in May to $248.2 million from $748.7 million in May 1996, the Economy Ministry said Friday.</p>
<p>Total income rose by $326.7 million from the same month last year to $1.77 billion.</p>
<p>The May shortfall compares with a $410.4 million deficit in April this year.  </p>
<p>Total spending in May was $2.02 billion, down from $2.19 billion in the same month last year.</p>
<p>((--Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0652))</p>
